":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110172.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #107864 \r\n\r\nWhen a disconnect event is generated from a call to `service()`, the field in the array where the disconnected peer should be is null. \r\n\r\nThe original bug report says this occurs during unclean disconnects but I found it will happen during clean disconnects as well. The problem was due to `_on_disconnect()` nulling the peer before it could be returned. Leaving out that line fixes the issue. The destructor for `ENetPacketPeer` should handle freeing the memory used by this peer when it's not needed. I've also modified `is_active()` so that the disconnected peer will still be considered inactive despite not being null.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110172/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110172/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}